  "pre_stated_readout": "Train recipe-matched DeBERTa seed43022 only if compute is free after higher-priority extent tasks and after the higher-dose qwen_pair_packed split has been considered. Score Wikipedia T/U/N by target class, natural-copy, compact rewrite T/U/N, and Entity against CLEAN. The removed ordinary-natural dose is small: 3508 tau=0.50 high-overlap pairs per 10M before splitting, reduced by 2591 pairs, about 7.8% of the 33291-pair designed compact intervention; a linear extrapolation from the designed DeBERTa compact effects would predict only around 0.06 nats on compact A_T and around 0.02 nats on Wikipedia target classes, near one-seed measurement floors. Target-form-separated signs if this lower-dose natural adjacency matters: splitting exact natural recurrence should lower natural-copy gain and may relieve source-absent changed-token cost, while splitting nonidentical natural adjacency should reduce true-source advantage on source-recurring restatement tokens. A small or null measurement mainly bounds sensitivity to ordinary-natural dose and relation quality, not the established high-dose compact locality result.",
